# tools/record/flows/example-app.flow
# Example flow: record the Workbooks Browser (Tauri/WebKitGTK Linux build).
# Run inside the Linux substrate:  tools/record/record record-flow tools/record/flows/example-app.flow
#
# Grammar (one verb per line):
#   app   -- CMD...   launch app on the virtual display
#   wait  <seconds>   pause
#   step  <shell>     run a driver step (xdotool / MCP client / curl) on $DISPLAY
#   shot  <out.png>   mid-flow still
#   note  <text>      log marker

note  launching the Workbooks Browser Linux build
# Replace with the real AppImage / deb-installed binary path inside the container:
app   -- /opt/workbooks/workbooks-browser
wait  3
shot  ./.rec/01-boot.png

note  open a workbook (synthetic events are invisible; prefer the embedded MCP)
# Native pointer driving (visible cursor) via xdotool:
step  xdotool mousemove 720 450 click 1
wait  1
shot  ./.rec/02-clicked.png

note  type into the focused field
step  xdotool type --delay 80 "hello workbooks"
wait  2
shot  ./.rec/03-typed.png

note  flow done — record stop + gif happen automatically
